      "id": 1,
      "text": "Green Hill was first settled before 1800 by John Cloyd and John Williamson, who moved from Nashville to escape smallpox.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green_Hill%2C_Tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Colonel John Donelson Jr. later built a summer home in Green Hill.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green_Hill%2C_Tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The community’s name may honor a former state treasurer of North Carolina or describe its location.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green_Hill%2C_Tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A post office operated in Green Hill from the 1830s until 1904, marking its 19th‑century civic life.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green_Hill%2C_Tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Green Hill’s early economy included a general store, hotel, tobacco processor, flour mill, and carding machine, reflecting a self‑sufficient rural hub.",
